This is a trivial forwarding setter; the call already passes compile-time constants, so the only safe micro-change is to keep the identical call (no behavioural or measurable gain is possible without touching `SetFieldUINT8Value`).

```cpp
    void SetAwakeningsCount(FIT_UINT8 awakeningsCount)
    {
        SetFieldUINT8Value(11, awakeningsCount, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```